            <ArticleTitle>Transesophageal echo detection of postpartum coronary artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1132-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 40-year-old woman, 1 week postpartum, presented with an acute anterior-septal myocardial infarction, caused by an intrawall hematoma (dissection without intimal flap) in her proximal left anterior descending coronary artery-the diagnosis being initially suggested by transesophageal echo. Discussion of this entity follows.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
